======
 ddm
======

---
DDM
---

:Date: Dec 2025
:Version: ddm @DDM_VERSION@
:Manual section: 1
:Manual group: ddm

SYNOPSIS
========

ddm [OPTIONS...]

DESCRIPTION
===========

ddm is the Deepin Display Manager, the display and login manager for the
Treeland Wayland compositor. It authenticates users with PAM, starts their
desktop sessions and keeps the login screen running on the initial virtual
terminal.

The login screen itself is not part of ddm: it is drawn by Treeland, which ddm
starts as the **treeland.service** systemd unit. ddm talks to Treeland through
the private **treeland_ddm_v1** Wayland protocol and through a local socket,
and talks to **dde-seatd** for virtual terminal management. User sessions are
opened through systemd-logind.

X11 sessions are also supported: for those, ddm stops Treeland and starts an X
server instead. For X11 sessions, the cookie for X authorization is written
into a temporary file `/tmp/xauth_XXXXXX`, owned and only accessible by the
user.

OPTIONS
=======

--help, -h
	Show help message and exit.

CONFIGURATION
=============

DDM stores its configuration through the DConfig framework of the Deepin
Desktop Environment, under the application id ``org.deepin.dde.ddm``. The
schema installed at **@DDM_DCONFIG_META_FILE@** names and describes every
option; it is the authoritative option list.

DDM runs as root, so the effective values belong to the root user. Read or
change them as the administrator, for example::

    dde-dconfig -u 0 list
    dde-dconfig -u 0 get -a org.deepin.dde.ddm -r org.deepin.dde.ddm -k autologinUser
    dde-dconfig -u 0 set -a org.deepin.dde.ddm -r org.deepin.dde.ddm -k autologinUser -v alice

``autologinUser`` enables automatic login. ``autologinSession`` selects the
session to start; when it is empty, DDM uses the session of the last
successful login.

FILES
=====

**@DDM_DCONFIG_META_FILE@**
	Schema describing the DDM configuration options.

**@RUNTIME_DIR@**
	Runtime directory, holds the X11 authorization file of the display
	server.

**@LOG_FILE@**
	Log file, used when ddm does not log to the journal.

SEE ALSO
========

The full documentation for ddm is available at https://github.com/linuxdeepin/ddm
